From 9f7924bab1368c81a5eace58203ed30ab9a6d9dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:11:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app): log file names, not paths; saturate log
 durations

Review items on PR #222: save/open/NC-write log lines name the file
only (logging::file_name), so a pasted log does not expose the user's
folder layout; generation and post durations go through
logging::elapsed_ms (u64::try_from, saturating at u64::MAX) instead of
`as_millis() as u64`. The logging suite now also asserts the full paths
are absent. Decision note in docs/decisions/163-tracing.md.

Refs #163

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
